# Vercel deploys the admin dashboard from this repo with Root Directory = web-admin, so the
# upload only needs that folder. Without this, `vercel --prod` from the repo root ships the
# whole monorepo (API, ML worker, mobile app, docs) to build one Next.js app.
/*
!/web-admin

# `!/web-admin` re-includes the whole folder, including `.env.local` — which Next loads *over*
# `.env.production` even in a production build. Deploying from the repo root would otherwise inline
# a developer's `http://localhost:5080` into the live bundle, and the build would still succeed.
# web-admin/.vercelignore says the same thing for the `cd web-admin && vercel --prod` route.
web-admin/.env.local
web-admin/.env*.local
